    "title": "Exquisitely decorated home of Victorian workman David Parr wins blue plaque",
    "summary": "David Parr was a Victorian labourer who spent his days applying William Morris's patterns to grand houses and Cambridge colleges. At night he covered his own Cambridge terrace house with designs of his own, and the home has now been awarded a blue plaque.",
