    "theme": "Victorian design and craft"
  },
  "headlines": [
    "Every Wall Became a Garden",
    "Morris by Day, Himself by Night",
    "A Workman's House of Wonder"
  ],
  "sublines": [
    "Victorian decorator David Parr papered mansions by day, then filled his own Cambridge terrace with patterns he designed.",
    "His modest house, covered in his own designs, has earned a blue plaque for its remarkable interiors.",
    "Paid to hang William Morris's patterns in grand rooms, a working man made a private palace at home."
